{"assets":["/statement-assets/4b8342987c08fce692c39718106a6b7ecebb410eb12ec0f9ceda8e579f5731c6.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"850","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Random Elections"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1024 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The presidential election is coming in Bearland next year! Everybody is so excited about this!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So far, there are three candidates, Alice, Bob, and Charlie. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" citizens in Bearland. The election result will determine the life of all citizens of Bearland for many years. Because of this great responsibility, each of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" citizens will choose one of six orders of preference between Alice, Bob and Charlie uniformly at random, independently from other voters."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The government of Bearland has devised a function to help determine the outcome of the election given the voters preferences. More specifically, the function is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/4b8342987c08fce692c39718106a6b7ecebb410eb12ec0f9ceda8e579f5731c6.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" (takes "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" boolean numbers and returns a boolean number). The function also obeys the following property: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"f(1 - x1, 1 - x2, ..., 1 - xn) = 1 - f(x1, x2, ..., xn)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Three rounds will be run between each pair of candidates: Alice and Bob, Bob and Charlie, Charlie and Alice. In each round, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xi"},{"kind":"text","text":" will be equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":", if "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th citizen prefers the first candidate to second in this round, and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":" otherwise. After this, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y = f(x1, x2, ..., xn)"},{"kind":"text","text":" will be calculated. If "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y = 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", the first candidate will be declared as winner in this round. If "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y = 0"},{"kind":"text","text":", the second will be the winner, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Define the probability that there is a candidate who won two rounds as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p"},{"kind":"text","text":". "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p·6n"},{"kind":"text","text":" is always an integer. Print the value of this integer modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109 + 7 = 1 000 000 007"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains one integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 20"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next line contains a string of length "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2n"},{"kind":"text","text":" of zeros and ones, representing function "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"f"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bk(x)"},{"kind":"text","text":" the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bit in binary representation of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th (0-based) digit of this string shows the return value of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"f(b1(i), b2(i), ..., bn(i))"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"f(1 - x1, 1 - x2, ..., 1 - xn) = 1 - f(x1, x2, ..., xn)"},{"kind":"text","text":" for any values of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1, x2, ldots, xn"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output one integer — answer to the problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n01010101\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"216\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n01101001\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"168\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In first sample, result is always fully determined by the first voter. In other words, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"f(x1, x2, x3) = x1"},{"kind":"text","text":". Thus, any no matter what happens, there will be a candidate who won two rounds (more specifically, the candidate who is at the top of voter 1's preference list), so "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p = 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", and we print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1·63 = 216"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"850E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/850/problem/E"}